  "summary_plain": "One page, five grand staves, thirty-four printed regions in 2/4 with no key signature. P001 is an opening one-eighth pickup: slurred right-hand A4 sixteenth to B4 sixteenth against a left-hand eighth rest, with treble over bass and 2/4. P009 is three eighth-note units before a thin-thin section double bar with no repeat dots; P010 is one eighth-note unit after that bar, two printed sixteenths. P034 is three eighth-note units before the thin-plus-thick final barline. Both staves open treble over bass. Eleven later left-hand clef glyphs are printed: treble at the ends of P003, P007, P016, P028 and P032; bass at the ends of P005, P009, P018 and P030; a cautionary treble at the end of P020; and a mid-bar bass inside P022 after the left-hand A3+C4 eighth, first governing E3 then F-sharp3 sixteenths. System-start clefs are reprints, including the system-4 left-hand treble reprint of the P020 cautionary. Geometry, capacities, and previous/first-event strings match the print and the proposed lock.",
